        ['Two fair dice are thrown and the scores are added. (a) Draw the sample space showing all possible totals. (b) Find the probability that the total is 10. (c) Find the probability that the total is greater than 10.', ['Sample space of 36 outcomes', '3 ways to get 10', 'P = 1/12', 'P(greater) = 1/12'], '(a) A 6 × 6 table of totals from 2 to 12 (36 outcomes). (b) There are 3 ways to get 10, so P = 1/12. (c) There are 3 totals greater than 10, so P = 1/12.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
