        ['Tickets for a school show cost GH₵ 15 for adults and GH₵ 6 for children. 120 tickets were sold and GH₵ 1,413 was collected. (a) Form two equations using a for adults and c for children. (b) Solve them to find how many of each ticket were sold. (c) Check your answer.', ['Two equations', 'Substitution or elimination', 'a = 77', 'c = 43', 'Check'], '(a) a + c = 120 and 15a + 6c = 1,413. (b) From the first, c = 120 − a. Substituting: 15a + 6(120 − a) = 1,413, so 9a = 693, a = 77 and c = 43. (c) 77 + 43 = 120 and 15 × 77 + 6 × 43 = 1,413.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
        ['Tickets for a school show cost GH₵ 15 for adults and GH₵ 8 for children. 116 tickets were sold and GH₵ 1,236 was collected. (a) Form two equations using a for adults and c for children. (b) Solve them to find how many of each ticket were sold. (c) Check your answer.', ['Two equations', 'Substitution or elimination', 'a = 44', 'c = 72', 'Check'], '(a) a + c = 116 and 15a + 8c = 1,236. (b) From the first, c = 116 − a. Substituting: 15a + 8(116 − a) = 1,236, so 7a = 308, a = 44 and c = 72. (c) 44 + 72 = 116 and 15 × 44 + 8 × 72 = 1,236.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
        ['Tickets for a school show cost GH₵ 15 for adults and GH₵ 5 for children. 112 tickets were sold and GH₵ 1,200 was collected. (a) Form two equations using a for adults and c for children. (b) Solve them to find how many of each ticket were sold. (c) Check your answer.', ['Two equations', 'Substitution or elimination', 'a = 64', 'c = 48', 'Check'], '(a) a + c = 112 and 15a + 5c = 1,200. (b) From the first, c = 112 − a. Substituting: 15a + 5(112 − a) = 1,200, so 10a = 640, a = 64 and c = 48. (c) 64 + 48 = 112 and 15 × 64 + 5 × 48 = 1,200.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
        ['Tickets for a school show cost GH₵ 25 for adults and GH₵ 6 for children. 70 tickets were sold and GH₵ 1,180 was collected. (a) Form two equations using a for adults and c for children. (b) Solve them to find how many of each ticket were sold. (c) Check your answer.', ['Two equations', 'Substitution or elimination', 'a = 40', 'c = 30', 'Check'], '(a) a + c = 70 and 25a + 6c = 1,180. (b) From the first, c = 70 − a. Substituting: 25a + 6(70 − a) = 1,180, so 19a = 760, a = 40 and c = 30. (c) 40 + 30 = 70 and 25 × 40 + 6 × 30 = 1,180.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
        ['Tickets for a school show cost GH₵ 15 for adults and GH₵ 4 for children. 73 tickets were sold and GH₵ 512 was collected. (a) Form two equations using a for adults and c for children. (b) Solve them to find how many of each ticket were sold. (c) Check your answer.', ['Two equations', 'Substitution or elimination', 'a = 20', 'c = 53', 'Check'], '(a) a + c = 73 and 15a + 4c = 512. (b) From the first, c = 73 − a. Substituting: 15a + 4(73 − a) = 512, so 11a = 220, a = 20 and c = 53. (c) 20 + 53 = 73 and 15 × 20 + 4 × 53 = 512.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
