        ['A cylindrical water tank has a radius of 14 cm and a height of 50 cm. Taking π = 22/7, find (a) its volume in cm³, (b) its capacity in litres, (c) its curved surface area, (d) its total surface area if it is closed at both ends.', ['Volume 30,800 cm³', 'Capacity 30.8 L', 'CSA 4,400 cm²', 'TSA 5,632 cm²'], '(a) V = 22/7 × 14² × 50 = 30,800 cm³. (b) 30,800 ÷ 1,000 = 30.8 litres. (c) 2 × 22/7 × 14 × 50 = 4,400 cm². (d) 4,400 + 2 × 22/7 × 14² = 5,632 cm².', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
        ['A cylindrical water tank has a radius of 21 cm and a height of 50 cm. Taking π = 22/7, find (a) its volume in cm³, (b) its capacity in litres, (c) its curved surface area, (d) its total surface area if it is closed at both ends.', ['Volume 69,300 cm³', 'Capacity 69.3 L', 'CSA 6,600 cm²', 'TSA 9,372 cm²'], '(a) V = 22/7 × 21² × 50 = 69,300 cm³. (b) 69,300 ÷ 1,000 = 69.3 litres. (c) 2 × 22/7 × 21 × 50 = 6,600 cm². (d) 6,600 + 2 × 22/7 × 21² = 9,372 cm².', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
        ['A cylindrical water tank has a radius of 21 cm and a height of 30 cm. Taking π = 22/7, find (a) its volume in cm³, (b) its capacity in litres, (c) its curved surface area, (d) its total surface area if it is closed at both ends.', ['Volume 41,580 cm³', 'Capacity 41.58 L', 'CSA 3,960 cm²', 'TSA 6,732 cm²'], '(a) V = 22/7 × 21² × 30 = 41,580 cm³. (b) 41,580 ÷ 1,000 = 41.58 litres. (c) 2 × 22/7 × 21 × 30 = 3,960 cm². (d) 3,960 + 2 × 22/7 × 21² = 6,732 cm².', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
        ['A cylindrical water tank has a radius of 7 cm and a height of 10 cm. Taking π = 22/7, find (a) its volume in cm³, (b) its capacity in litres, (c) its curved surface area, (d) its total surface area if it is closed at both ends.', ['Volume 1,540 cm³', 'Capacity 1.54 L', 'CSA 440 cm²', 'TSA 748 cm²'], '(a) V = 22/7 × 7² × 10 = 1,540 cm³. (b) 1,540 ÷ 1,000 = 1.54 litres. (c) 2 × 22/7 × 7 × 10 = 440 cm². (d) 440 + 2 × 22/7 × 7² = 748 cm².', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
    ],
